From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] input-capture: Disable the session when its EIS client disconnects

A client can close its EIS connection while capture is active. Relying on
an empty seat binding to disable the session is racy: the disconnect
notification need not be preceded by that event. Capture then remains
active and the existing input-capture/disconnect test waits indefinitely
for the Deactivated signal.

Disable the session before dropping the client and seat. This releases
capture and emits Deactivated while the session is active. An already
closed session has already performed this cleanup.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/backends/meta-input-capture-session.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-input-capture-session.c
@@ -420,6 +420,9 @@
       break;
 
     case EIS_EVENT_CLIENT_DISCONNECT:
+      /* A disconnected client cannot release its active capture itself. */
+      if (session->state != INPUT_CAPTURE_STATE_CLOSED)
+        meta_input_capture_session_disable (session);
       g_clear_pointer (&session->eis_seat, eis_seat_unref);
       g_clear_pointer (&session->eis_client, eis_client_unref);
       break;
